# Build output only.
/target/

# ⚠ Cargo.lock is NOT ignored, and must never be.
#
# It pins the entire transitive dependency tree to exact versions with a
# SHA-256 checksum each, which is the control that stops the npm-style attack
# the workspace manifest's policy is about. A binary crate committing its lock
# is also cargo's own recommendation. Deleting or ignoring this file is the
# supply-chain regression — not editing a version number.
!Cargo.lock
